1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,665
The court went dark on our

2
00:00:01,665 --> 00:00:03,111
last possession. Before I

3
00:00:03,111 --> 00:00:04,470
could even see, someone

4
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:06,047
yelled the new kid's name.

5
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:07,095
Eli lived across from the

6
00:00:07,095 --> 00:00:09,085
park. He'd spent three nights

7
00:00:09,085 --> 00:00:10,365
watching through the fence

8
00:00:10,365 --> 00:00:11,669
before he asked to play.

9
00:00:11,669 --> 00:00:12,827
Earlier that evening, he

10
00:00:12,827 --> 00:00:14,437
brought his own ball. He

11
00:00:14,437 --> 00:00:15,917
asked which hoop we used,

12
00:00:15,917 --> 00:00:17,028
like there was a rule.

13
00:00:17,028 --> 00:00:18,176
When the lights went out, my

14
00:00:18,176 --> 00:00:19,886
friend pointed at him. Eli

15
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:21,338
had been nearest to the gate.

16
00:00:21,338 --> 00:00:22,666
I was about to say the same

17
00:00:22,666 --> 00:00:24,376
thing. Then he picked up his

18
00:00:24,376 --> 00:00:25,746
bag and walked off without

19
00:00:25,746 --> 00:00:26,439
arguing.

20
00:00:26,439 --> 00:00:27,667
Someone said we could finish

21
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:29,467
tomorrow. I went to the gate

22
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:30,677
to check if the park was

23
00:00:30,677 --> 00:00:31,361
closing.

24
00:00:31,361 --> 00:00:32,519
There was a yellow plug

25
00:00:32,519 --> 00:00:34,279
hanging out of the box. I

26
00:00:34,279 --> 00:00:35,239
could just see it under the

27
00:00:35,239 --> 00:00:36,008
street lamp.

28
00:00:36,008 --> 00:00:37,536
I pushed it back in. The

29
00:00:37,536 --> 00:00:39,326
lights came on one at a time,

30
00:00:39,326 --> 00:00:40,686
and the ball rolled across

31
00:00:40,686 --> 00:00:41,194
the court.

32
00:00:41,194 --> 00:00:42,652
From the gate I could see Eli

33
00:00:42,652 --> 00:00:44,562
heading toward the crosswalk.

34
00:00:44,562 --> 00:00:45,882
I grabbed the ball and went

35
00:00:45,882 --> 00:00:46,541
after him.

36
00:00:46,541 --> 00:00:48,089
I held it out. He took it

37
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,419
with one hand and kept

38
00:00:49,419 --> 00:00:50,489
looking at the paint on the

39
00:00:50,489 --> 00:00:51,100
pavement.

40
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:52,118
I told him I'd found the

41
00:00:52,118 --> 00:00:53,888
plug. He asked if I'd told

42
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:55,704
the others too. I hadn't.

43
00:00:55,704 --> 00:00:57,412
So I went back to the court.

44
00:00:57,412 --> 00:00:58,792
My friend was already picking

45
00:00:58,792 --> 00:01:00,012
teams like nothing had

46
00:01:00,012 --> 00:01:00,598
happened.

47
00:01:00,598 --> 00:01:02,146
I told him about the plug.

48
00:01:02,146 --> 00:01:03,476
Then I told him I'd almost

49
00:01:03,476 --> 00:01:05,796
blamed Eli too. Nobody picked

50
00:01:05,796 --> 00:01:06,904
a team after that.

51
00:01:06,904 --> 00:01:08,232
My friend put his hand down

52
00:01:08,232 --> 00:01:09,392
and walked to the gate with

53
00:01:09,392 --> 00:01:10,902
me. We called Eli back

54
00:01:10,902 --> 00:01:11,485
together.

55
00:01:11,485 --> 00:01:13,023
He looked up this time. He

56
00:01:13,023 --> 00:01:14,443
put his bag on the bench and

57
00:01:14,443 --> 00:01:15,593
came through the gate with

58
00:01:15,593 --> 00:01:16,218
the ball.

59
00:01:16,218 --> 00:01:17,186
We let him take the first

60
00:01:17,186 --> 00:01:19,226
shot. He bent his knees,

61
00:01:19,226 --> 00:01:20,416
looked once at the rim, and

62
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:21,222
let it go.

63
00:01:21,222 --> 00:01:22,340
It hit the front of the rim

64
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:24,090
and came right back. For a

65
00:01:24,090 --> 00:01:26,115
second, nobody said anything.

66
00:01:26,115 --> 00:01:27,743
My friend caught it. Instead

67
00:01:27,743 --> 00:01:29,123
of taking his turn, he threw

68
00:01:29,123 --> 00:01:30,008
it back to Eli.

69
00:01:30,008 --> 00:01:31,216
Eli asked if he could move a

70
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:33,316
step closer. We all backed up

71
00:01:33,316 --> 00:01:34,326
to give him room.

72
00:01:34,326 --> 00:01:35,584
The lights stayed on until

73
00:01:35,584 --> 00:01:37,374
closing. When we played again

74
00:01:37,374 --> 00:01:39,214
the next day, Eli was the one

75
00:01:39,214 --> 00:01:40,260
picking teams.
